# WayPoint frontend configuration.
#
# Copy to `frontend/.env` and adjust. Everything here is optional — the defaults
# work for local development and for the single-container deploy.

# Where the FastAPI API lives.
#
# Leave this EMPTY unless the site and the API are on different origins. Empty
# means "same origin", which is correct in both of these cases:
#
#   - local dev:   Vite proxies /api and /uploads to http://127.0.0.1:8000
#                  (see vite.config.ts), so the browser never leaves the origin.
#   - production:  one container serves the API *and* the built SPA.
#
# Only a split deploy needs it — e.g. the site on Vercel and the API on
# Render/Railway/Fly, where it must be the API's absolute origin with no
# trailing slash:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://waypoint-api.onrender.com
#
# If the site loads but shows no data, this is the first thing to check. The API
# reports whether the browser's origin is allowed at /health/config.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Optional. Swap the inline SVG mark for your own artwork in public/.
# VITE_LOGO_URL=/logo.png